// "case on X, exhaustive b/c R" in one line; remainders written as the user's reason
let n be an integer. wts n^3 - n is divisible by 3
case on n mod 3, exhaustive b/c every integer leaves remainder 0, 1, or 2 when divided by 3
case n mod 3 = 0. then 3 divides n, so 3 divides n^3 - n.
case n mod 3 = 1. then 3 divides n - 1, so 3 divides n^3 - n = (n - 1)n(n + 1).
case n mod 3 = 2. then 3 divides n + 1, so 3 divides n^3 - n.
exhaustive, so 3 divides n^3 - n
qed
